    "lawCode": "Add §1399-ddd, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6073\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public health law, in relation to\nthe regulation of electronic distributors of vaping products\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nEnacts rules to ensure that online retailers of vaping products take\nnecessary steps to prevent minors from purchasing their goods and rules\nregarding proper labelling of such products when shipped from an online\nretailer.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. adds a new section 1399-ddd to the Public Health Law and\nprovides for conspicuous labeling of shipped vaping products. Provides\nthat online retailers take necessary steps to keep minors from purchas-\ning their products including warning labels, signed acknowledgements and\nphoto ID requirements. Gives the department of health oversight of such\nretailers and authority to suspend their licenses if requirements are\nnot met. Makes each violation of such provisions a civil offense punish-\nable by a fine of $5,000 to $25,000 and up to 6 months license suspen-\nsion for the first offense, a fine of $10,000 to $30,000 and up to three\nyears license suspension for a second offense within three years, and\nlicense suspension up to five years for a third offense within five\nyears. Establishes a committee within the department with the authority\nto inspect, grade, and monitor online distributors of vaping products.\n\nSection 2. is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPreventing minors from buying vaping products requires regulation of all\npotential marketplaces where such products are sold. Without rules\ngoverning their operation, online retailers present a real and clear\nopportunity for negligence and a back door to minor sales. This legis-\nlation will close many of those loopholes and punish violators as appro-\npriate.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome law.\n",
